Third-party content
-------------------

The effect parameter descriptions in `spec/effects.toml`, the tables generated
from them in `docs/effects.md`, and `FxSlot::description` under the crate's
`descriptions` feature, are taken from section 9.3 of the DeepMind 12 User
Manual, published by Music Tribe. They are reproduced so that a program can tell
a musician what a parameter does, which is what the protocol data on its own
cannot convey.

The program parameter descriptions in `spec/parameters.toml`, which reach
`docs/midi-spec.md` and `ParamId::description`, are not from the manual. They
are written for this project against what the rest of the specification records,
and a parameter whose behaviour it does not establish has none rather than a
guessed one.

The colours in `spec/layout.toml` were measured from the effect panels pictured
in the same section: four colours per effect, taken by where they sit in the
picture and how much of it they cover. The result is twelve bytes per effect
and no artwork. Which control each panel uses - knob, fader or numeric display -
was read off the same pictures, one word per effect. The drawings in
`docs/diagrams/fx/` are generated from those two facts and from the parameter
tables; they are not traced from, and do not resemble, Behringer's panels.

Everything else in `spec/` is factual interface data: parameter numbers, byte
offsets, names, ranges, units, value lists, and where the synthesizer's own
display puts a control. Facts about how a device behaves are not themselves
creative work, and recording them is what makes an independent implementation
possible.

If Music Tribe or Behringer would prefer the effect descriptions or the sampled
colours were not reproduced here, open an issue and they will be removed.
Nothing else in this repository depends on either: both are optional fields, the
descriptions are behind a feature that is off by default, and the library works
without them.
